From d9dad7f9c0be3f09f8b656292091dce4ac87ba32 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 02:15:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(web): keep Today's KPI cards live and honest
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Key the session, win-rate and streak requests on dbRev so every
  game card refreshes on games:changed, as Games in range and Ladder
  Pulse already did. /v1/me/mmr stays unkeyed (one SC2Pulse call per
  Pulse ID).
- Rename "Games today" to "Today's session": "6 games" with today's
  "4W 2L" record (or "0 games" / "No games yet today"), replacing the
  "Keep the streak alive" hint that was wrong during a losing run.
- Loading shows a dash and a skeleton hint; a failed request shows a
  dash and "Couldn't load · Retry" (aria-busy while it runs) instead of
  a fake 0. A failed MMR request no longer says "Add a Pulse ID".
- Phone grid: the lead card spans both columns (1, 2, 2 instead of an
  orphan); the route and layout skeletons match.
- The MMR empty hint links to Settings → Profile's Pulse ID help, which
  now opens when the address points at it.
- The Win rate timeframe menu moves to its own file and gets full menu
  keyboard support: focus the selected item on open, wrapping arrows,
  Home/End, Esc back to the button, Tab closes; it opens toward the
  middle of the screen on phones.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
