From 30518e7e52a24bc5c78ff1ce6370e5ab048dc1cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 02:15:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix(web): apply the Default tab only when a session
 starts on /app

Today used to redirect to the saved default tab from the client, once
per tab via sessionStorage, so clicking Today could bounce you away
(and every visit bounced when storage was blocked).

- AnalyzerFrame sets a browser-session cookie (sc2_app_session, no
  Max-Age) when any /app page first mounts.
- The /app page reads the preference on the server only while that
  cookie is missing (1.5 s timeout; any failure shows Today) and
  redirects before render, after the ?opponent and ?tab redirects.
  Clicking Today later, or opening /app/maps first, shows Today.
- TodayView drops its redirect effect and the extra misc request.
- defaultTabRedirect also reads a section slug ("maps").
- The Settings hint says when the default tab applies.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KG8e5a59qtUDJJY3Fm1hxC
